cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software in your research, please cite the associated
  publication and the specific software version using the metadata below.

type: software

title: >-
  Counterfactual Single-Trial Dynamics Reveal How Premotor Manifold
  Geometry Reconciles Coupled Control with Independent Races

abstract: >-
  This repository provides the implementation of a causal,
  context-modulated Deep Markov Model developed to investigate
  neural population dynamics in the dorsal premotor cortex (PMd)
  of macaques performing a countermanding task. The model extracts
  a memoryless three-dimensional latent flow field from neural
  activity and predicts reaction-time distributions in a zero-shot
  setting. It enables paired in silico counterfactual simulations
  with identical noise realizations, allowing the investigation
  of single-trial coupling between action initiation and cancellation.
  The associated study shows how a tilted decision boundary on a
  shared premotor manifold can couple single-trial outcomes while
  preserving aggregate behavior consistent with the Independent
  Race Model.

